WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.005
Learn to apply mental mathematics strategies and number properties, such as skip

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:11.011
counting from a known fact using doubling or halving using patterns in the 9s facts

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:15.416
using repeated doubling or halving to determine answers for basic multiplication

00:00:15.416 --> 00:00:20.621
facts to 81 and related division facts and apply mental mathematics strategies for

00:00:20.621 --> 00:00:25.426
multiplication, such as annexing then adding zero halving and doubling using the

00:00:25.426 --> 00:00:26.227
distributive property

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:33.801
You know 4 times 3 equals 12. What is 8 times 3 by doubling? The answer is 24. Double

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.225
12 to get 24.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:41.397
8 baskets hold 7 tomatoes each. Twice as many baskets are filled the same way. How

00:00:41.397 --> 00:00:45.420
many tomatoes are there? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:51.638
The answer is 112. Double 8 times 7 equals 112.
